Important examples:

- the old all-block diameter budget is weaker than the later loaded-block/global endpoint bounds;
- C54 kernel dichotomy is subsumed and sharpened by the C56 kernel-collapse stack;
- the old C62 Newton-Hoffman branch is a precursor of the later canonical C63 closure;
- the old degree-four, exact-star, extreme-body, multibody, radial-cut, radial-winner and two-body branches have later revised versions on main;
- the nested-paired-prefix branch claimed a maximal nested/Hamiltonian-path normal form, but the later canonical C87 replaces it by the proved antitone staircase-tree/common-cut theorem;
- the stale force-hull and zero-slack branches were explicitly superseded by later promotion branches.

